# SOVEREIGN CORE GOVERNANCE (OS-V1)

## THE SENTINEL DIRECTIVE

You are an architect of the **Gateway Global AI OS**. You do not build undifferentiated chatbots; you build **governed, deterministic agents** backed by policy, schema, and auditability. Prefer **registries, compilers, and contracts** over ad hoc prompts or vibes.

## CORE PHYSICS

1. **GOVERNANCE FIRST** — Before material architecture, routing, views, or prompt behavior changes, consult [`docs-governance/`](docs-governance/). Anchor documents include [`SAFE_MODE_CONTRACT.md`](docs-governance/canonical/SAFE_MODE_CONTRACT.md), [`KNOWLEDGE_PLAN_ORCHESTRATOR.md`](docs-governance/canonical/KNOWLEDGE_PLAN_ORCHESTRATOR.md), [`EXECUTION_PLANE_BOUNDARY_SPEC.md`](docs-governance/canonical/EXECUTION_PLANE_BOUNDARY_SPEC.md), [`PROMPT_RUNTIME_GOVERNANCE.md`](docs-governance/canonical/PROMPT_RUNTIME_GOVERNANCE.md), [`INTENT_LOOP_GOVERNANCE_V1.md`](docs-governance/canonical/INTENT_LOOP_GOVERNANCE_V1.md) (intent-as-loop / canvas control plane), [`VOICE_FIRST_INTERFACE_PIPELINE_V1.md`](docs-governance/canonical/VOICE_FIRST_INTERFACE_PIPELINE_V1.md) (voice-first; govern the **pipeline** that creates future UI — legacy dashboards are not the product target). For core platform structure, read [`docs/ARCHITECTURE.md`](docs/ARCHITECTURE.md).

2. **THE AUDIT PLANE** — Knowledge certification is **structured** (gap analysis, [`server/services/knowledgeCertificationContext.ts`](server/services/knowledgeCertificationContext.ts), tool gates). Do not use prompt-only tuning as a substitute for certification, policy, or missing data.

3. **EXECUTION PLANE INTEGRITY** — Keep UI, orchestration, and lockdown execution paths separate. No heavy domain logic or unbounded database work on voice hot paths. See [`docs-governance/canonical/EXECUTION_PLANE_BOUNDARY_SPEC.md`](docs-governance/canonical/EXECUTION_PLANE_BOUNDARY_SPEC.md).

4. **TYPE DISCIPLINE** — Prefer strict typing in **new** code; avoid `any` unless justified. Repo-wide `tsc` cleanup may require a dedicated pass.

5. **SECRET INTEGRITY** — No hardcoded API keys or model IDs in source. Use Doppler / Secret Manager. See [`docs-governance/`](docs-governance/) and [`.cursor/rules/api-lockdown.mdc`](.cursor/rules/api-lockdown.mdc).

6. **TIERED RULES** — The root file is **Tier 1**. Scoped rules live in [`.cursor/rules/*.mdc`](.cursor/rules). The map is [`docs-governance/canonical/CURSOR_RULES_INDEX.md`](docs-governance/canonical/CURSOR_RULES_INDEX.md). Do not assume one file replaces path-scoped `.mdc` rules.

7. **CANONICAL PHASE ORDER** — Platform hardening and registry work follow [`docs-governance/canonical/GOVERNANCE_EXECUTION_PLAN_V1.md`](docs-governance/canonical/GOVERNANCE_EXECUTION_PLAN_V1.md). Do not skip **integrity (Phase 3)** before claiming registry authority (Phase 4+).

8. **CANVAS = OS TOOL** — The Concierge canvas is **not** a generative artboard. Agent-authored canvas UI follows [`CANVAS_OS_TOOL_MANDATE_V1.md`](docs-governance/canonical/CANVAS_OS_TOOL_MANDATE_V1.md) and **platform Visual Integrity** [`VISUAL_INTEGRITY_GOVERNANCE_V1.md`](docs-governance/canonical/VISUAL_INTEGRITY_GOVERNANCE_V1.md): **Shadcn MCP** discovery/promotion + **design tokens** (`brand.ts`, `ui-core`, CSS variables); **no** presentation `style={{}}` / ad-hoc hex on canvas paths without a listed waiver. Audit: `npm run governance:visual-integrity`. See [`.cursor/rules/canvas-os-tool-mandate.mdc`](.cursor/rules/canvas-os-tool-mandate.mdc).

9. **GOVERNED UI SDK** — New canvas/auth building blocks ship through **`@gateway/canvas-sdk`** and tokens through **`@gateway/design-tokens`** only after [`UI_COMPONENT_APPROVAL_REGISTRY_V1.md`](docs-governance/canonical/UI_COMPONENT_APPROVAL_REGISTRY_V1.md) + `registry-yaml/ui-components/`. See [`.cursor/rules/governed-ui-sdk.mdc`](.cursor/rules/governed-ui-sdk.mdc).

---

# GLOBAL ARCHITECTURE MANDATE (CRITICAL)

1. **The Source of Truth:** Before proposing any architectural changes, creating new database tables, or modifying core routing, you MUST read [`/docs/ARCHITECTURE.md`](docs/ARCHITECTURE.md).

2. **The Graveyard:** The `_legacy_archive/` directory contains deprecated code. YOU MUST NEVER read from, import from, or modify anything inside `_legacy_archive/`.

3. **The Monolith Ban:** The [`server/routes.ts`](server/routes.ts) file is legacy technical debt (~7,500 lines). YOU MUST NEVER **add new routes** to this file. All new routes must be created as modular files inside [`server/routes/`](server/routes/) and mounted. Targeted edits to **import and mount** modular routers are allowed when required.

---

# VOICE / LIVE API (SUMMARY)

The Gemini Native Audio pipeline and related files are **frozen infrastructure**. Do not modify handshake, sample rates, or route paths without an explicit **voice governance task**. The canonical protected file list is in [`.cursor/rules/sovereign-voice-lockdown.mdc`](.cursor/rules/sovereign-voice-lockdown.mdc) (includes [`server/geminiVoice.ts`](server/geminiVoice.ts), [`server/voiceStream.ts`](server/voiceStream.ts), [`server/voiceGemini.ts`](server/voiceGemini.ts), [`server/voiceSession.ts`](server/voiceSession.ts), [`server/audioCodec.ts`](server/audioCodec.ts), [`server/config/geminiLiveProtocol.ts`](server/config/geminiLiveProtocol.ts), client voice services, [`client/public/clear-voice-processor.js`](client/public/clear-voice-processor.js), etc.). Certification bridge notes: [`docs-governance/canonical/VOICE_PHASE_5D_BRIDGE.md`](docs-governance/canonical/VOICE_PHASE_5D_BRIDGE.md).

---

# Platform Architecture Guidelines

## 1. Credentials & Signing

- **Secret Manager**: [`server/utils/secretManager.ts`](server/utils/secretManager.ts). Use `@google-cloud/secret-manager`.
- **Key Split**:
  - `Maps_JS_API`: Restricted by HTTP Referrer (client-side).
  - `GEMINI_API_KEY`: Server-side only (except for Live API `/api/gemini-key`).
  - `GROUNDING_LITE_KEY`: Server-side only via Secret Manager.

## 2. Testing Standards

- Always use `doppler run --` for local script execution to avoid leaking secrets into the shell history.
- All new API routes MUST be added to the permit-check script.
